ot\in K$, then $\pi(t_{m})
eq 1$, so $t_{m}$ acts on $EK_{0}	imes ET^n$ with no fixed-points. If $t_{m}
ot\in \Omega_{p}$ for any $p\in P$, then $t_{m}$ acts on $(T^m	imes P)/\Omega$ with no fixed-points. Since $K\cap \Omega_{p}=1$ for all $p\in P$, the diagonal action of $T^m$ on $(EK_{0}	imes ET^n)	imes (T^m	imes P)/\Omega$ is free. So the projection  egin{equation} p_{2}: W	imes_{T^m}(T^m	imes P)/\Omega ightarrow (EK_{0}	imes ET^n)	imes_{T^m} (T^m	imes P)/\Omega \end{equation} is a fiber bundle with fiber $ET^m$. So  egin{equation} W	imes_{T^m}(T^m	imes P)/\Omega \stackrel{h.e.}{\sim} (EK_{0}	imes ET^n)	imes_{T^m} (T^m	imes P)/\Omega. \end{equation} Combining \eqref{eq:p1} and \eqref{eq:p2} completes the proof.

So the projection
\begin{equation} p_{2}: W\times_{T^m}(T^m\times P)/\Omega \rightarrow (EK_{0}\times
ET^n)\times_{T^m} (T^m\times P)/\Omega
\end{equation}
is a fiber bundle with fiber $ET^m$. So
